# apps/web — Next.js 16

Next.js **16.2**, React **19**, Tailwind **4** via `@workspace/ui`. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and root `AGENTS.md` before unfamiliar APIs.

## Structure

```
app/layout.tsx     ClerkProvider (root)
app/(dashboard)/   auth.protect() in layout
app/sign-in|sign-up/   Clerk catch-all
app/healthz/       Docker/K8s health (GET JSON)
components/        domain UI (qc/, surveys/, admin/, layout/)
features/          colocated components, hooks, lib
lib/api/           axios client + types
stores/app-store.ts   useAuthStore (permissions from /users/me)
providers/         Clerk token bridge, React Query
proxy.ts           Next 16 edge auth (NOT middleware.ts)
```

## Next 16 specifics

- Route `params` / `searchParams` are `Promise<…>` — `await` in RSC, `use()` in client.
- Auth edge file is **`proxy.ts`**, not `middleware.ts`.
- `experimental.authInterrupts: true` — use `forbidden()` for 403 UX.
- Dev script uses `next dev --webpack` (Turbopack avoided in monorepo dev).

## Auth layers

| Layer  | File                          | Role                                                 |
| ------ | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Edge   | `proxy.ts`                    | `clerkMiddleware()` — session context only           |
| Shell  | `(dashboard)/layout.tsx`      | `auth.protect()` + `GET /users/me` + permission gate |
| Client | `providers/app-providers.tsx` | `setApiTokenGetter` from `useAuth().getToken`        |

Product authorization uses **Nest permissions** (`permissions` on profile), not Clerk roles. Server fetch must unwrap envelope via `lib/auth/unwrap-api-profile.ts`.

## API client

- Use `lib/api/client.ts` (`apiGet`, `apiPost`, …) or `hooks/use-api.ts`.
- Envelope: `{ success, message, data, errors }` — throw when `!success`.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:4000`).
- React Query: `staleTime: 30_000`, `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`.
- Gate queries: `enabled: isLoaded && isSignedIn && hasPermission(...)`.

## UI

- Import from `@workspace/ui/components/*`, `cn` from `@workspace/ui/lib/utils`.
- Do not add local shadcn primitives — extend `@workspace/ui`.
- Validators from `@workspace/validation` where shared.

## Never

- Import `@workspace/database`, Prisma, or Nest code.
- Call `@aws-sdk/*` or talk to S3/MinIO directly — uploads/downloads go through Nest presigned URLs (`lib/api/client.ts`).
- Put `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` or `DATABASE_URL` in client components or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Create `middleware.ts`.
